{
 "_comment": "Back (solder side) silkscreen, v1.2. Placed on B.Cu at board (100, 100); KiCad mirrors it, so local x = 100 - board x, local y = board y - 100 (and +x local is the viewer's LEFT on the real board). H1 pins at local x = +13, H2 at -13, pin k at y = -26 + 2.54(k-1); J1 (anchored on pin 1): GND x 5.0, DIN 2.5, 5V 0.0, all at y 25. Layout: the URL in the top band (no separate wordmark - the ball carries the brand); a 42 mm golf ball centred on the socket area (it runs past the pin columns; the pads punch clean rings through it), lit from the viewer's upper left (dimples are cup shadows that fade out toward the highlight), with the SignPainter 'OSSTempo' script and a '1' knocked out of it, Titleist-style, 18 mm wide, in the clear strip between the headers; 'Designed in Austin, TX' in the bottom band. Arrows mark every pin to solder: H1.2 GND, H1.8 D5, H2.1 5V, H2.2 GND, J1 x3, plus H1.1, H1.15, H2.8, H2.15 for mechanical stability (no legend, by choice). Every pad has a keepout (socket pads are 2.0 mm on v1.2); the base art drops dimples near labels and pads. Generate with --board <built .kicad_pcb>: the tool then clips to the board outline and adds a keepout around every pad, via and hole it finds there.",
